<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka 1996 inflation at 15.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka 1996 inflation at 15.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka's inflation as measured by the consumer price index was 15.9 percent in 1996, sharply up from previous year's 7.7 percent, the Central Bank said in its annual report released on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said a rise in food prices accounted for more than 80 percent of the increase in inflation.</p>
<p>&quot;A sharp increase in the average international price of wheat compelled the government to raise the domestic price of wheat flour to reduce the strain on the budget,&quot; the report said.</p>
</text>
